/**
 * terrainReport.ts: the words of the terrain intelligence report and the
 * Contour Studio PDF in each export language.
 *
 * One row per phrase: English, Spanish (Mexico), Portuguese (Brazil), French,
 * German. English is the source and a row with a language missing fails the
 * build. The sentences other modules write (reasons, warnings, provenance) are
 * matched to their English row by terrain/export/reportWords.ts. A sentence
 * with no row keeps the whole report in English, and a test reads the modules
 * that write them and fails on a sentence with no row.
 *
 * Parameters: `{n}` is a figure, with its unit if it has one, and takes the
 * number style; `{t_x}` is a phrase with a row of its own; `{j_x}` is a list of
 * such phrases and `{J_x}` one that opens a sentence; `{c_x}` is one word
 * copied exactly and `{u_x}` text copied exactly. A row whose key has a
 * capital prefix and an underscore (`SQ_`) is a word of one field only and is
 * not matched in running text.
 *
 * Drafts until a geomatics reviewer signs them off (`reviewed` in
 * languages.ts); until then every report says so.
 */
